x.q('composition_host_and_regime_validation',0,38,42,'fn_composition_contract','Fail closed if local vector/evaluator/rule/hook/operator host differs in function/vector/source/target/schema/owning declaration refs. Every regime declares kind, role, order, authority, input/output carriers and applicable evidence. F_D may own closure; F_P may construct/diagnose/repair/rank/evidence; F_H may be present/deferred/absentia. Non-F_D cannot claim closure. Explicit standards/policy inputs govern construction/admission/closure/replay/fallback/escalation/observability; differing identity is non-equivalent unless declared migration/supersession admits it.',exceptions=['Declared migration or supersession policy may admit standards/policy identity change.'])
x.q('carrier_assurance_closure_context',0,44,48,'fn_composition_contract','Preserve selected source/target carriers, applicable target contract ref/digest, payload projections and closure preconditions; evaluate target under carrier identity, not files/prose/generic payload. Preserve applicable edge assurance ref/digest, required evidence, gates and projections; findings under composition identity are not closure law. Closure names F_D function/predicate, required/rejection evidence, replay projection and closure event. Success/self-assessment/tests/report shape/gap absence/transport never imply closure.')
x.c('composition_optimization',0,50,50,'Declared deterministic optimization','Replacing a probabilistic/mixed path with deterministic path requires source composition ref/digest, replacement ref, positive and negative equivalence cases, equivalence projection and invalidation policy.')
x.q('composition_public_carriers',0,52,62,'fn_composition_contract','Templates/defaults are visible config or published GTL, never hidden hardcode/null contracts/prompts/parser fallback/lazy replay reads. Consuming events, ledgers, assurance, envelopes, observations and pressure packages carry selected ref/digest or causal selection ref; same events replay same identity. Before design-method closure preserve an Irreducible Architectural Carrier Set and structural diagram; parser/admission/projection/exports derive from it, not helpers/prompts. fn<A,B>.C and stage.C notation remains validated/traversed/admitted declaration truth, not a new target/closure/ledger/controller.')
x.c('declared_stage_set',0,64,74,'Declared ordered C stage set','GTL/Product identify lawful hosts/hooks/policies/read-model intent; ABG admits candidates/evaluations, events, ledgers, assurance/traversal, closure and replay. HoG traverses exact admitted stage order; ABG admits/resumes each stage call/frame, regime/implementation, invocation/result and exposes replay truth for next bind.')
x.q('stages_before_disposition',0,66,74,'declared_stage_set','Assurance/disposition/continuation/closure may be admitted only after result-bearing stage and required downstream binds. HoG/ABG cannot synthesize absent stages, force three-stage chain, rename domain role or count runtime admission as authored membership.')
x.q('plugin_categories_and_human_boundary',0,76,80,'fn_composition_contract declared_stage_set','Participating plugins declare compute-stage category/means/purpose, selected composition at invocation and authority-denial flags. Current categories are transform/candidate construction, evaluate/candidate evaluation, consequence/projection and external human callout. F_H work surface is external; ABG may emit/admit boundary events/carriers but callouts cannot directly write events/ledgers/transitions/replay/closure. Observer/hooks use evaluate; reject malformed/legacy category names instead of mapping them to authority.')
x.c('declared_evaluation_set',0,82,100,'Declared evaluation set and stage law','GTL declares evaluation membership/dependencies and stable sequential/parallel batches; HoG traverses these; implementations perform tasks; ABG admits results and derives ledgers/order/assurance/set projections. Every authored C stage follows this law, including transform/evaluate/consequence when present; scalar hooks reduce to one task.')
x.q('evaluation_fail_closed_and_no_planner',0,82,100,'declared_evaluation_set','ABG cannot plan/schedule evaluation, synthesize a loop or reorder GTL. Plugins may compute outcomes within selected boundaries but cannot write ledgers, choose traversal, transition or close. Required rules fail closed if absent/stale/malformed/contradictory/rejected or mismatched composition/digest/regime contribution. HoG consumes only admitted output at next declared bind; runtime transitions cannot satisfy authored cardinality/conservation.')
x.c('traversal_unit',0,102,109,'TraversalUnit','Monadic traversal atom under one admitted program, selected function, workspace binding and compute basis. ABG admits its result and next-unit/same-unit retry/graph-span or public re-entry/reprice/yield/block/gap-stop/non-admit/terminal disposition; neither unit nor callable replaces program.')
x.q('bind_chain_obligation_conservation',0,109,109,'traversal_unit','Conserve program, selected-action/current-intent, immutable workspace, basis and lineage. Every bind carries/accounts for intent,lineage,obligations,target-carriers,materialization/output,pressure,staged-authority,admission-strength and downstream terminal pressure. Unit close clears refs only through admitted realization, refinement, named downstream deferral, block,re-entry,reprice,no-close preservation or terminal projection; scalar close cannot erase obligation vector. Divergent/undeclared predicates for staged pressure vs materialization authority make materializing unit nonconformant.')
x.c('sufficient_construction_intent',0,111,111,'Sufficient ConstructionIntent','Before dispatch for newly selected traversal/product/artifact materialization, admit or validate one sufficient intent from admitted NextActionProjection and lineage, binding program/action/published membership/target obligations/workspace/invocation authority/basis.')
